        "content": [
          {
            "tool_use_id": "toolu_011KDHsMXdsYf7xNtM4LxL6E",
            "type": "tool_result",
            "content": "#### Spotlight\n\nWhile a step shows, the window is dimmed, as an inset panel dims it, but for a cut-out around the part the step points at, with 4 pixels of room and corners rounded 6 pixels, outlined in the theme's accent, so that part reads as lit. The cut-out moves to each step's part, easing between them over 200 milliseconds, and follows it if the window is resized.\nBeside it sits the callout, a card on the theme's raised surface with corners rounded 8 pixels, a border, and a shadow, at most 320 pixels wide, placed on whichever side of the part has room, with a small pointer toward it, and never off the window. It holds the step's title, its text as a paragraph or two, \"Step N of M\", muted, and along its bottom a Back button, disabled on the first step, a primary Next button, reading \"Done\" on the last step, and a \"Skip tour\" link at the left. It is drawn in the theme's roles, in dark mode and light.\nWhile a step shows, only the callout and the part lit take the mouse, and clicks on the dimmed window do nothing, so the walkthrough is never left by accident. <Escape> skips the tour, as Skip tour does, and <Enter>, while Next is enabled, goes to the next step.\n\n#### Steps",
            "is_error": false
          }
        ]
      },
